face-image: img/portraits/goerdeler.jpg

= New State Consolidation

Goodlake, the <i>Reichskommissar</i> of Heartland, has announced his resignation in favor of Chancellor Goodryke, likely under pressure from both the chancellor and Staal as they move to consolidate power into the chancellery. Goodlake, ever the conservative, sympathizes with these goals and steps down before DuFour can force the issue.

It is clear this is part of Goodryke’s wider plan for a "New State"—a centralized, anti-democratic regime ruled by aristocrats and the rich. The upcoming Heartland elections have now been postponed indefinitely.

- @surrender: How blatant can Goodryke be!?

